// Techniques: knowledge held by populations (each cell's people know a set).
//
// A technique can be invented where its requirements are met: the
// techniques it builds on (`requires`, listed earlier in this file), crops or
// herds the people keep (`requires_crops`, `requires_herds`), one of some
// domesticated species (`requires_species`), and the place (`where`):
//   river   a river runs through the cell        coast   it touches the sea
//   water   river or coast                       dry     under 900 mm of rain
//   hills   above 600 m                          forest  a forest biome
// People build know-how toward it by doing what it grows from: `practice`
// weighs what they do (each about 0 to 1, see systems/technology.hpp):
//   foraging, hunting, fishing, farming, herding   how they get their food
//   crowding        people / what the land feeds (Boserup: pressure on land
//                   brings irrigation, terraces, ploughs)
//   storing         food stored a person
//   towns           townspeople around them, per 10,000
//   trade           goods traded around them (per 500 a year)
//   redistribution  surplus passing through the hands of chiefs, priests and
//                   kings: towns and food brought in, kept account of at a
//                   realm's seat (temple and palace bookkeeping led to writing)
//   rule            the size of their realm
// Each year know-how grows by practice x sqrt(people / 10,000) (at most 4) x
// (0.5 + innovation) x the culture's affinity (1 + sum of weight x 2 x
// (trait - 0.5) over `affinity`, at least 0.1) / `practice_years`, and by
// learning from neighbours who use it; it fades over 1,000 years (30 in
// communities under 500). At 1 they know it: so a technique is invented
// where its practice is intense and lasting enough, after about
// `practice_years` of full practice by a community of 10,000. Populations
// under 500 people forget a little each year (the Tasmanian effect: Henrich
// 2004), and techniques whose requirements are gone fade.
//
// `requires_goods`: goods that must be on the cell's market (made there or
// brought by trade) to invent or keep it: smelters need ore, bronze-smiths
// copper and tin. Cut off from them, the craft fades.
//
// `start_chance`: share of the starting peoples who already know it.
//
// Effects (add up over techniques, where each applies):
//   crop_yield      farmland crops x (1 + sum)
//   herd_yield      herds x (1 + sum)
//   forage          land foraging (plants and game) x (1 + sum)
//   aquatic         fish and shellfish x (1 + sum)
//   harvest_buffer  share of a bad harvest's shortfall made good (mixed crops
//                   and fields, famine foods, kin), and storage: a cell may
//                   keep (0.25 + 3 x sum) years of food (EconomySystem stores)
//   famine          famine mortality x (1 + sum), so negative is better
//   contact         learning from and teaching neighbours x (1 + sum)
//   administration  how far a capital's rule reaches x (1 + sum): writing,
//                   bureaucracy and roads let states hold distant land
//   land_transport  overland carrying cost / (1 + sum): horses, carts, roads
//   water_transport river and sea carrying cost / (1 + sum); any at all
//                   (canoes) lets people cross the sea to nearby coasts
//   military        each soldier's fighting strength x (1 + sum): bows,
//                   horses, chariots, copper and bronze weapons
//
{
  "version": 1,
  "techniques": [
    {"id": "bow", "name": "Bow and arrow", "practice": {"hunting": 1, "farming": 0.3}, "practice_years": 820, "start_chance": 0.5,
     "affinity": {"plant_reliance": -0.5},
     "effects": {"forage": 0.08, "military": 0.15}},
    {"id": "nets", "name": "Fishing nets and weirs", "where": "water", "practice": {"fishing": 1}, "practice_years": 900, "start_chance": 0.4,
     "affinity": {"mobility": -0.5},
     "effects": {"aquatic": 0.25}},
    {"id": "canoes", "name": "Dugout canoes", "where": "water", "practice": {"fishing": 1}, "practice_years": 900, "start_chance": 0.3,
     "effects": {"aquatic": 0.1, "contact": 0.2, "water_transport": 0.25}},
    {"id": "pottery", "name": "Pottery", "practice": {"storing": 0.5, "fishing": 0.5, "farming": 0.5}, "practice_years": 2150, "start_chance": 0.05,
     "affinity": {"storage": 1.0, "mobility": -1.0},
     "effects": {"famine": -0.2, "forage": 0.03, "harvest_buffer": 0.1}},
